---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Ayomiposi Sotomi"
  description="Final-year Cybersecurity student. Freelance web developer. Security-minded human."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl lg:max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-medium text-text md:text-5xl">
      About
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral mt-10 max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm Ayomiposi Sotomi, a final-year Cybersecurity student at the
        Federal University of Technology, Akure (FUTA). I also freelance as
        a web developer. I've lived in Nigeria all my life, and when I want
        to understand a system, my first instinct is usually to take it
        apart.
      </p>
      <p>
        My main interest is defensive security: the work of keeping systems
        running and making them harder to compromise. Alongside that, I
        build websites for clients and tinker with a homelab. Right now,
        it's a Docker-based media and automation setup, but I plan to move
        it to a dedicated Proxmox server. Self-hosting has taught me more
        than most tutorials ever did. Eventually, I'd like to start a
        cybersecurity consulting firm.
      </p>
      <p>
        Growing up, the hardest lessons weren't technical. They were about
        expectations. You reach one goal, then another one is already
        waiting. If you're not careful, you can spend your life chasing the
        next thing without deciding what "enough" means for yourself.
        Learning to say no helped more than anything else. That's a big part
        of why I care about self-expression, and why I try to give people
        room before judging them.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is my attempt to keep all of those interests in one
        place. You'll find occasional essays about things I keep turning
        over in my head, write-ups from homelab experiments and other
        projects, and a Now page. It saves me from scattering everything
        across Substack, GitHub, and social media. I don't think of myself
        as a writer, exactly. Mostly, I write to make sense of my own
        thoughts and pay attention to ordinary things.
      </p>
      <p>
        I want this to feel more like a quiet garden than a portfolio. The
        point is to show the process, not only the polished final result.
        Some posts will be about finished projects. Others will be about
        half-built experiments, mistakes, and things that didn't work.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like to see what I'm building or want to get in touch, you
        can find me on{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/BlackJRoot" class="text-link hover:text-accent">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>